# Judgements

Γ ⊦ [α] t₀ ≐ t₁ ⇒ T    // Given core context Γ and a surface proof infer the core equation LHS, RHS and type
Γ ⊦ [α] t₀ ≐ t₁ ⇐ T    // Given core context Γ, core type T and a surface proof infer the core equation LHS, RHS
Γ ⊦ [ᾱ] ē₀ ≐ ē₁ ⇐ Δ    // spine equation, against a TELESCOPE Δ over Γ: a record's body, a QIIT's arguments (LISTS)
[ᾱ] e˲₀ ≐ e˲₁ : Γ ⇒ Δ norm  // normal-substitution equation, into a CONTEXT Δ: the arguments of a reference x[e˲] (LISTS)
Γ ctx                     // Γ is a well-formed context
Σ ⊢ I item                // the item I extends the signature Σ (the entry points)
Γ ⊦ [φ] 𝔽₀ ≐ 𝔽₁ poly ℓ        // polynomial equation proof at level ℓ, synthesising both sides
Γ ⊦ [ᾱ] Δ₀ ≐ Δ₁ tel ℓ         // telescope equation proof, synthesising both sides and the LEAST level ℓ

# Notation

// A proof written with ONE side, Γ ⊦ [α] a ⇐ A (likewise ⇒),
// means Γ ⊦ [α] a₀ ≐ a₁ ⇐ A with a₀ ≡β a₁ (the join is checked), and a
// stands for a₁. Γ ⊦ t ⇐ T and Γ ⊦ t ⇒ T abbreviate Γ ⊦ [t] t ≐ t ⇐ T and
// Γ ⊦ [t] t ≐ t ⇒ T: a term with no proof leaf is its own reflexivity
// proof, the one-sided case α = t. A surface piece a rule names in a
// premise (a motive C, a carrier a, a witness type T) denotes its core
// elaboration where the conclusion uses it. A premise Γ ⊦ [ρ] ⋆ ⇐ P, P a
// proposition, asks for ANY proof at P and disregards its sides: a
// hypothesis ☐ᵢ proves ☐ᵢ ≐ ☐ᵢ at P and serves there. Only a conclusion
// mints ⋆. A TYPE is a term at a SORT: a universe 𝒰 of the foundation's
// Syntax, Ω or a 𝕌ℓ, with its level |𝒰|. So "T is a type" is Γ ⊦ T ⇒ 𝒰,
// and an equation of types is an equation at a sort. There is no
// judgement of types, and no judgement of type equations, beside the two
// above.

# Syntax

// What a line of a rule may be. The proofs α and the judgements J are the
// kernel's. Everything else is the foundation's Syntax, repeated here until
// that document is in this format.

//! nova: x l l̄ 𝒰 𝒰̄ Σ I Γ Δ σ e˲ ē t
//! level: ℓ
//! tos: 𝕤 𝕔 Φ 𝔄 𝕥 𝔽
//! proof: α ᾱ φ

x ::= <signature-entry-identifier>
l ::= <label>
𝕤 ::= <sort-name>
𝕔 ::= <constructor-name>
l̄ ::= · | l l̄
ℓ ::= 0 | ℓ ⊔ ℓ | (ℓ) | |𝒰|
𝒰 ::= Ω | 𝕌ℓ | 𝕌ᵢ
𝒰̄ ::= · | 𝒰, 𝒰̄
Σ ::= ε | Σ I
I ::= (Γ ⊦ x : t) | (Γ ⊦ x ≔ t : t) | (Γ ⊦ x ≔ Φ qsig ℓ)
Γ, Δ ::= ε | Γ ▷ t
Δ ::= ε | t ◁ Δ | Δ[σ] | ⟦𝔄⟧ᵗ | ⟦Φ⟧ᴰ
σ ::= id | ↑ | ↑ⁿ | e˲ | σ, t | σ, ē
e˲ ::= · | e˲, t | (e˲, t)
ē, θ, ι, d̄, m̄ ::= · | t, ē | (t, ē) | ēᴰ

t, a, b, e, f, h, p, q, r, s, u, v, w, x, z, A, B, C, R, T ::= x[e˲]
    | ☐ᵢ | 𝒰 | 𝟘 | 𝟙 | ℕ | ⋆ | () | Z | S t | (t)
    | t → t | t × t | t ⊎ t | t / t | t ≡ t ∈ t | ∥t∥
    | λ t | t t | let t t | t, t | t.π₁ | t.π₂
    | Rec l̄ Δ | ⟨l̄ ↪ ē⟩ | ⟨l̄ ↪ t.l₀, …, t.lₙ₋₁⟩ | t.l
    | inj₁ t | inj₂ t | ⊎-elim t t t | 𝟘-elim t | ℕ-elim t t t
    | class t | quot-elim t t
    | x[e˲].𝕤 ē | x[e˲].𝕔 ē | x[e˲].𝕤-elim ē ē t
    | ν 𝔽 | out t | corec 𝔽 t t
    | t[σ] | Γ‖ᵢ | (t / l̄ ↪ Δ)‖ᵢ | ⌊𝔽⌋(t) | map_𝔽 t t | lift_𝔽(t) | ⟦𝕥⟧ | ē(𝕤) ē t

𝔽, 𝔾 ::= 𝕏 | K t | 𝔽 × 𝔽 | 𝔽 ⊎ 𝔽 | t × 𝔽 | t → 𝔽
Φ ::= ⬦ | Φ ▷ 𝔄 | Φ[σ]
𝔄, 𝔎 ::= U | El 𝕥 | t ⇛ 𝔄 | El 𝕥 ⇛ 𝔄 | 𝔄[σ] | 𝔄[𝕥] | Φ‖ᵢ
𝕥, 𝕦, 𝕝, 𝕣 ::= ⬡ᵢ | 𝕥 t | 𝕥 𝕥 | λ 𝕥 | 𝕥 ≡ 𝕥

α, β, γ, κ, λ, ρ, τ, φ, ω, θ, ι, π, χ ::= ☐ᵢ
    | 𝒰 | 𝟘 | 𝟙 | ℕ | () | Z | S α
    | α → α | α × α | α ⊎ α | α / α | α ≡ α ∈ α | ∥α∥ | Rec l̄ ᾱ
    | λ α | α α | let α α | α, α | α.π₁ | α.π₂ | ⟨l̄ ↪ ᾱ⟩ | α.l
    | inj₁ α | inj₂ α | ⊎-elim 𝒰 t α α α | 𝟘-elim α | ℕ-elim 𝒰 t α α α
    | class α | quot-eq α α α | quot-elim 𝒰 t α α α
    | reify α | reflect α | squash α | unsquash α α α
    | irrel α α | prop-irrel α α α | propext α α α α
    | lift α | restrict α α α | conv α α | (α : t)
    | x ᾱ | δ x e˲ | α ; α | α ⁻¹
    | η→ α | η× α | ηRec α
    | ν φ | out α | corec 𝔽 (s : t. α) α
    | ην 𝔽 (s : t. t) (s. t) α t | coind t t (x y. t) t (x y h. t)
    | x[ᾱ].𝕤 ᾱ | x[ᾱ].𝕔 ᾱ | x[e˲].𝕤-elim 𝒰̄ ᾱ ᾱ α | x[e˲].𝕔 ē
ᾱ, π̄, δ̄ ::= · | α, ᾱ | ᾱ, α
φ, ψ ::= 𝕏 | K α | φ × φ | φ ⊎ φ | α × φ | α → φ

J ::= Γ ctx | Σ ⊢ I item | I ∈ Σ
    | Γ ⊦ [α] t ≐ t ⇒ t | Γ ⊦ [α] t ≐ t ⇐ t
    | Γ ⊦ [α] t ⇒ t | Γ ⊦ [α] t ⇐ t | Γ ⊦ t ⇒ t | Γ ⊦ t ⇐ t
    | Γ ⊦ [ᾱ] ē ≐ ē ⇐ Δ | Γ ⊦ ē ⇐ Δ
    | [ᾱ] e˲ ≐ e˲ : Γ ⇒ Γ norm | e˲ : Γ ⇒ Γ norm
    | Γ ⊦ [φ] 𝔽 ≐ 𝔽 poly ℓ | Γ ⊦ 𝔽 poly ℓ
    | Γ ⊦ [ᾱ] Δ ≐ Δ tel ℓ
    | l ∈ l̄ | l ≠ l | l̄ distinct | |l̄| = |ᾱ|
    | 𝒰 sort | 𝒰 ≤ 𝒰 | 𝒰̄ targets Φ
    | t ≡β t | 𝔄 ≡β 𝔄 | t = t
    | Γ ⊦ Φ qctx ℓ | Γ ; Φ ⊦ 𝔄 qty ℓ | Γ ; Φ ⊦ 𝕥 ⇒ 𝔄 | Γ ; Φ ⊦ 𝕥 ⇐ 𝔄
    | Φ(𝕤) = 𝔄 | Φ(𝕔) = 𝔄 | 𝔄 ends El 𝕥 | 𝔄 ends El (𝕥 ≡ 𝕥) at 𝕥

# Conventions

// * A non-linear metavariable occurrence, or a former pattern (A → B, A × B,
//   t₀ ≡ t₁ ∈ T, …) in an input position, means equality modulo substitution
//   and β — weak-head β for a pattern, full β for a comparison. "β" is every
//   computation rule: β, the ι-rules, let-β, record-β, ν-β, QIIT-β. NEVER δ:
//   definitions unfold only through the proof former δ x. Every comparison
//   runs under a FUEL budget (equality reflection makes β-normalisation of a
//   well-typed term diverge under an inconsistent hypothesis); exhaustion is
//   rejection, so the checker is total.

// * NO δ FOR EXPOSURE EITHER. A pattern input (λ against a Π, a quot-elim
//   scrutinee against a quotient, ⋆ against a prop) is matched after
//   weak-head β only; a reference at the head is STUCK, and the term is
//   rejected unless an annotation ((conv t α) : T) exposes the shape, α a
//   chain of δ leaves naming each unfolding at its path (the annotation
//   rule, modal section). The reason: whnf-δ in
//   the checker would fix ONE unfolding strategy in the trusted base — the
//   producer would have to predict it step for step, its spellings would
//   leak into every downstream type and report, and its one wasteful case
//   (unfolding a scrutinee that then fails to make ι fire, leaving a larger
//   stuck term) could never be improved without changing what the checker
//   accepts. With δ explicit, over-normalisation is a PRODUCER quality —
//   visible as proof size, fixable by a better strategy or a lemma, never a
//   checker semantics. The producer should unfold PROGRESS-ONLY: the head
//   while it yields a former, a scrutinee only if ι then fires, rolled back
//   otherwise; the emitted chain is the shortest δ-sequence to the shape.
//   Without δ, β-normal forms are bounded by the written term's own redexes:
//   every blow-up the corpus shows is δ, and it now happens on the untrusted
//   side and is recorded.

// * SORTS ARE CUMULATIVE, Ω ≤ 𝕌₀ ≤ 𝕌₁ ≤ …: a proposition is a small type, a
//   small type is a large one. Cumulativity enters through exactly two proof
//   forms, lift and restrict (the modal section) — never silently — and acts
//   at the ROOT only: A → Ω is not A → 𝕌₀ (write λx. f x). Levels are
//   literals: no level polymorphism; a statement over (A : 𝕌₀) lives at 𝕌₁.
//   A former INFERS its least sort (the arithmetic on ℓ ⊔ ℓ′ below) and is
//   used at any higher one through lift; the checker never guesses a
//   universe.

// * Ω HAS NO CODE BELOW 𝕌₁: Ω ⇒ 𝕌₁ and never Ω ⇒ 𝕌₀, so A → Ω is a 𝕌₁ type
//   for every A (Cantor stays a theorem; the effective topos refutes Ω : 𝕌₀,
//   a program cannot tell two propositions apart, while validating every
//   p : Ω at 𝕌₀). Individual propositions ARE 𝕌₀ codes, by Ω ≤ 𝕌₀. Every
//   𝕌ℓ's equality is thereby MIXED: structural on the formers, extensional
//   (propext) on the proposition cluster; an equation across the clusters is
//   underivable by absence.

// * ELIMINATORS NAME THEIR SORT: the 𝒰 on ℕ-elim, ⊎-elim, quot-elim and the
//   QIIT eliminator is the sort the motive lands in, an INPUT the motive is
//   checked at, never computed from it. 𝒰 = Ω is where well-definedness and
//   coherences close by irrelevance.

# The entry points: contexts, items, the signature Σ

// Σ is a list of ITEMS, each closed over its own CONTEXT Δ:
//   (Δ ⊦ x : T) ∈ Σ           a DECLARATION (an assumption, a hole, a lemma's statement)
//   (Δ ⊦ x ≔ t : T) ∈ Σ       a DEFINITION
//   (Δ ⊦ x ≔ Φ qsig ℓ) ∈ Σ    a QIIT SIGNATURE: a qiit-context Φ over its parameters Δ, at its level ℓ
// Every rule below is relative to Σ. The checker is entered one item
// at a time, each read against the whole of Σ before it; an accepted
// item is appended, and nothing else ever extends Σ.

----- (ctx-empty)
ε ctx

Γ ctx      Γ ⊦ A ⇒ 𝒰
--------------------- (ctx-ext)
Γ ▷ A ctx

Δ ctx      Δ ⊦ T ⇒ 𝒰
-------------------------- (sig-decl)
Σ ⊢ (Δ ⊦ x : T) item
// A declaration: a statement that is a type at some sort.

Δ ctx      Δ ⊦ T ⇒ 𝒰      Δ ⊦ [α] t ⇐ T
----------------------------------------- (sig-def)
Σ ⊢ (Δ ⊦ x ≔ t : T) item
// A definition: the producer hands over a PROOF α at T; its right side is
// the definiens the kernel records (a plain term is its own proof; a lemma
// is a definition of ⋆ at an equation type, its proof a reify …).

Δ ctx      Δ ⊦ Φ qctx ℓ
------------------------------ (sig-qsig)
Σ ⊢ (Δ ⊦ x ≔ Φ qsig ℓ) item
// A QIIT signature: a qiit-context, checked ONCE, here, at the level ℓ it
// names. A former of it carries the NAME x and arguments for Δ (the QIIT
// section); no core term contains a qiit-context.

# Lists: normal substitutions, telescopes, spines

// Two shapes, the foundation's. A CONTEXT grows at its inner end, and a
// NORMAL SUBSTITUTION into it is built the same way: the parameters of an
// item of Σ, and the arguments of a reference to it. A TELESCOPE over Γ
// is read from its outer end, each entry binding in the rest, and a SPINE
// against it likewise: a record's entries and its body, a QIIT arity and
// its arguments. A one-sided list (e˲ : Γ ⇒ Δ norm, Γ ⊦ ē ⇐ Δ) is one
// whose proofs' sides β-join, entry by entry.

// The syntax of normal substitutions e˲, telescopes Δ and spines ē, and
// the operations on them — Γ · Δ, ↑Δ, Δ[σ], the derived snoc Δ ▷ A and
// the instantiation X[ē] — are the foundation's (Syntax; Rules (tel);
// the QIIT section's plumbing). Only their checking rules are stated
// here.

---------------------- (sub-norm-empty)
[·] · ≐ · : Γ ⇒ ε norm

[ᾱ] e˲₀ ≐ e˲₁ : Γ ⇒ Δ norm
Γ ⊦ [β] t₀ ≐ t₁ ⇐ A[e˲₁]
---------------------------------------------- (sub-norm-ext-cong)
[ᾱ, β] (e˲₀, t₀) ≐ (e˲₁, t₁) : Γ ⇒ Δ ▷ A norm
// The new entry at its type instantiated by the RIGHT substitution built
// so far.

----------------- (sp-empty)
Γ ⊦ [·] · ≐ · ⇐ ε

Γ ⊦ [α] e₀ ≐ e₁ ⇐ A
Γ ⊦ [ᾱ] ē₀ ≐ ē₁ ⇐ Δ[id, e₁]
---------------------------------------- (sp-ext-cong)
Γ ⊦ [α, ᾱ] (e₀, ē₀) ≐ (e₁, ē₁) ⇐ A ◁ Δ
// The head at the telescope's head, the rest against the rest
// instantiated at the RIGHT head.

# Π-type

Γ ▷ A ⊦ [α] f₀ ≐ f₁ ⇐ B
--------------------------- (el-pi-i)
Γ ⊦ [λ α] λf₀ ≐ λf₁ ⇐ A → B

Γ ⊦ [α] f₀ ≐ f₁ ⇒ A → B
Γ ⊦ [β] e₀ ≐ e₁ ⇐ A
----------------------------------- (el-pi-e)
Γ ⊦ [α β] f₀ e₀ ≐ f₁ e₁ ⇒ B[id, e₁]

# Σ-type

Γ ⊦ [α] p₀ ≐ p₁ ⇒ A × B
----------------------------------- (el-sigma-e₁)
Γ ⊦ [α .π₁] p₀ .π₁ ≐ p₁ .π₁ ⇒ A

Γ ⊦ [α] p₀ ≐ p₁ ⇒ A × B
-------------------------------------------- (el-sigma-e₂)
Γ ⊦ [α .π₂] p₀ .π₂ ≐ p₁ .π₂ ⇒ B[id, p₁ .π₁]

Γ ⊦ [α] a₀ ≐ a₁ ⇐ A
Γ ⊦ [β] b₀ ≐ b₁ ⇐ B[id, a₁]
----------------------------------------- (el-sigma-i)
Γ ⊦ [α, β] (a₀, b₀) ≐ (a₁, b₁) ⇐ A × B

# Record type

// Rec l̄ Δ: a telescope Δ over Γ with a LABEL per entry, the labels a
// parallel list l̄ (telescopes and spines: LISTS above). A
// label is INERT — compared syntactically, never
// bound, never substituted for — so a record's body is an ordinary
// spine of Δ and its proof an ordinary spine proof. The formation rule
// is with the other formers (𝕌-type), η with the leaves. In the concrete
// syntax a label doubles as the binder name of its entry, a projection
// is the postfix ρ .l, and the record has two spellings: ⟨l ↪ α, …⟩
// inline and the keyword record, a field per line, in block layout.

Γ ⊦ [ᾱ] ē₀ ≐ ē₁ ⇐ Δ
---------------------------------------------- (el-rec-i)
Γ ⊦ [⟨l̄ ↪ ᾱ⟩] ⟨l̄ ↪ ē₀⟩ ≐ ⟨l̄ ↪ ē₁⟩ ⇐ Rec l̄ Δ
// The labels are the TYPE's, in its order: a literal at another label list
// is rejected, never permuted. Distinctness and the lengths are the input
// type's; the spine fixes |ᾱ| = |Δ|.

Γ ⊦ [ρ] r₀ ≐ r₁ ⇒ Rec l̄ Δ      l ∈ l̄
---------------------------------------------- (el-rec-e)
Γ ⊦ [ρ .l] r₀.l ≐ r₁.l ⇒ (r₁ / l̄ ↪ Δ)‖ₗ
// l ∉ l̄ is rejection. The type is the FIELD TYPE of l at the right
// record, the foundation's walk from the head, the record standing for its
// own earlier components:

(t / l l̄ ↪ A ◁ Δ)‖ₗ  = A
(t / l′ l̄ ↪ A ◁ Δ)‖ₗ = (t / l̄ ↪ Δ[id, t.l′])‖ₗ      l′ ≠ l

// COMPUTATION is el-rec-beta, inside "modulo β": ⟨l̄ ↪ ē⟩.lᵢ ⇝ eᵢ, by
// lookup of the label in the literal. No type is consulted.

# ⊎-type

Γ ⊦ [α] a₀ ≐ a₁ ⇐ A
------------------------------------- (el-sum-i₁)
Γ ⊦ [inj₁ α] inj₁ a₀ ≐ inj₁ a₁ ⇐ A ⊎ B

Γ ⊦ [β] b₀ ≐ b₁ ⇐ B
------------------------------------- (el-sum-i₂)
Γ ⊦ [inj₂ β] inj₂ b₀ ≐ inj₂ b₁ ⇐ A ⊎ B

𝒰 sort
Γ ⊦ [τ] t₀ ≐ t₁ ⇒ A ⊎ B
Γ ▷ A ⊎ B ⊦ C ⇐ 𝒰
Γ ▷ A ⊦ [λ] u₀ ≐ u₁ ⇐ C[↑, inj₁ ☐₀]
Γ ▷ B ⊦ [ρ] v₀ ≐ v₁ ⇐ C[↑, inj₂ ☐₀]
-------------------------------------------------------------------- (el-sum-e)
Γ ⊦ [⊎-elim 𝒰 C λ ρ τ] ⊎-elim u₀ v₀ t₀ ≐ ⊎-elim u₁ v₁ t₁ ⇒ C[id, t₁]

# Quotient type

Γ ⊦ [α] a₀ ≐ a₁ ⇐ A
----------------------------------------- (el-quot-i)
Γ ⊦ [class α] class a₀ ≐ class a₁ ⇐ A / R

Γ ⊦ [α] a ⇐ A      Γ ⊦ [β] b ⇐ A      Γ ⊦ [ρ] ⋆ ⇐ R[id, a, b]
------------------------------------------------------ (el-quot-eq)
Γ ⊦ [quot-eq α β ρ] class a ≐ class b ⇐ A / R
// Related representatives, equal classes.

𝒰 sort
Γ ⊦ [κ] q₀ ≐ q₁ ⇒ A / R
Γ ▷ A / R ⊦ B ⇐ 𝒰
Γ ▷ A ⊦ [φ] f₀ ≐ f₁ ⇐ B[↑, class ☐₀]
Γ ▷ A ▷ A[↑] ▷ R ⊦ [ω] f₁[↑³, ☐₂] ≐ f₁[↑³, ☐₁] ⇐ B[↑³, class ☐₂]   // f₀'s well-definedness follows through φ;
------------------------------------------------------------------------ (el-quot-e) //   at 𝒰 = Ω, ω is irrel
Γ ⊦ [quot-elim 𝒰 B φ ω κ] quot-elim f₀ q₀ ≐ quot-elim f₁ q₁ ⇒ B[id, q₁]

# 𝟘-type

Γ ⊦ [α] t₀ ≐ t₁ ⇐ 𝟘
---------------------------------------- (el-zero-e)
Γ ⊦ [𝟘-elim α] 𝟘-elim t₀ ≐ 𝟘-elim t₁ ⇐ A

# 𝟙-type

-------------------- (el-one-i)
Γ ⊦ [()] () ≐ () ⇐ 𝟙

# ℕ-type

----------------- (el-nat-z)
Γ ⊦ [Z] Z ≐ Z ⇐ ℕ

Γ ⊦ [α] t₀ ≐ t₁ ⇐ ℕ
------------------------- (el-nat-s)
Γ ⊦ [S α] S t₀ ≐ S t₁ ⇐ ℕ

𝒰 sort
Γ ▷ ℕ ⊦ A ⇐ 𝒰
Γ ⊦ [α] z₀ ≐ z₁ ⇐ A[id, Z]
Γ ▷ ℕ ▷ A ⊦ [β] s₀ ≐ s₁ ⇐ A[↑², S ☐₁]
Γ ⊦ [τ] t₀ ≐ t₁ ⇐ ℕ
------------------------------------------------------------------ (el-nat-e)
Γ ⊦ [ℕ-elim 𝒰 A α β τ] ℕ-elim z₀ s₀ t₀ ≐ ℕ-elim z₁ s₁ t₁ ⇒ A[id, t₁]

# ≡-type

Γ ⊦ [α] t₀ ≐ t₁ ⇒ T
--------------------------------- (el-eq-i)
Γ ⊦ [reify α] ⋆ ≐ ⋆ ⇒ (t₀ ≡ t₁ ∈ T)
// The equation REIFIED as a proposition; written ⌜α⌝ inline.

Γ ⊦ [α] ⋆ ⇒ t₀ ≡ t₁ ∈ T
--------------------------- (el-reflect)
Γ ⊦ [reflect α] t₀ ≐ t₁ ⇒ T
// The proposition REFLECTED to its equation; written ⌞α⌟ inline. The two
// are inverse: reflect (reify α) proves what α proves, and
// reify (reflect h) ≐ h by irrelevance.

# The sorts as terms

----------------------- (ty-univ)
Γ ⊦ [𝕌ℓ] 𝕌ℓ ≐ 𝕌ℓ ⇒ 𝕌ℓ₊₁

------------------ (ty-prop)
Γ ⊦ [Ω] Ω ≐ Ω ⇒ 𝕌₁
// And NOT ⇒ 𝕌₀ (CONVENTIONS): Ω is the one type that is
// not a code at the level of its elements.

# 𝕌-type: the formers

// The formers INFER their least sort; the arithmetic is on the sorts the
// parts infer. Two rules for →: into a universe (the level is the join)
// and into Ω (a proposition whatever the domain — the one impredicative
// rule, and the reason Ω is a sort of its own rather than a universe).
// A bound part is compared over the RIGHT-hand domain of the binder.

Γ ⊦ [α] A₀ ≐ A₁ ⇒ 𝒰
Γ ▷ A₁ ⊦ [β] B₀ ≐ B₁ ⇒ 𝕌ℓ
------------------------------------------------ (ty-pi)
Γ ⊦ [α → β] (A₀ → B₀) ≐ (A₁ → B₁) ⇒ 𝕌(|𝒰| ⊔ ℓ)

Γ ⊦ [α] A₀ ≐ A₁ ⇒ 𝒰
Γ ▷ A₁ ⊦ [β] B₀ ≐ B₁ ⇒ Ω
------------------------------------------------
Γ ⊦ [α → β] (A₀ → B₀) ≐ (A₁ → B₁) ⇒ Ω
// Impredicative.

Γ ⊦ [α] A₀ ≐ A₁ ⇒ 𝒰₁
Γ ▷ A₁ ⊦ [β] B₀ ≐ B₁ ⇒ 𝒰₂
--------------------------------------------------- (ty-sigma)
Γ ⊦ [α × β] (A₀ × B₀) ≐ (A₁ × B₁) ⇒ 𝕌(|𝒰₁| ⊔ |𝒰₂|)
// A product of propositions is a small TYPE, not a proposition: p ∧ q is
// ∥p × q∥.

// A telescope is compared from its head, each entry a type equation
// over the RIGHT-hand entries before it, and INFERS its least level: the
// join of the sorts its entries infer, 0 at the empty telescope (|Ω| = 0:
// a proposition costs nothing). This is the foundation's Γ ⊦ Δ₀ ≐ Δ₁ tel ℓ
// at the least such ℓ; a higher one is reached at the former, by lift.

------------------- (tel-lvl-empty)
Γ ⊦ [·] ε ≐ ε tel 0

Γ ⊦ [α] A₀ ≐ A₁ ⇒ 𝒰
Γ ▷ A₁ ⊦ [ᾱ] Δ₀ ≐ Δ₁ tel ℓ
--------------------------------------------- (tel-lvl-ext-cong)
Γ ⊦ [α, ᾱ] A₀ ◁ Δ₀ ≐ A₁ ◁ Δ₁ tel (|𝒰| ⊔ ℓ)
// At the least level.

l̄ distinct      |l̄| = |ᾱ|
Γ ⊦ [ᾱ] Δ₀ ≐ Δ₁ tel ℓ
--------------------------------------- (ty-rec)
Γ ⊦ [Rec l̄ ᾱ] Rec l̄ Δ₀ ≐ Rec l̄ Δ₁ ⇒ 𝕌ℓ
// ONE label list on both sides. A record is at the level of its telescope;
// a record of propositions is a small TYPE, as a product is.

Γ ⊦ [α] A₀ ≐ A₁ ⇒ 𝒰₁
Γ ⊦ [β] B₀ ≐ B₁ ⇒ 𝒰₂
--------------------------------------------------- (ty-sum)
Γ ⊦ [α ⊎ β] (A₀ ⊎ B₀) ≐ (A₁ ⊎ B₁) ⇒ 𝕌(|𝒰₁| ⊔ |𝒰₂|)

Γ ⊦ [α] A₀ ≐ A₁ ⇒ 𝒰
Γ ▷ A₁ ▷ A₁[↑] ⊦ [ρ] R₀ ≐ R₁ ⇐ Ω
--------------------------------------- (ty-quot)
Γ ⊦ [α / ρ] (A₀ / R₀) ≐ (A₁ / R₁) ⇒ 𝕌|𝒰|
// The relation slot is Ω: a code is not a proposition.

------------------ (ty-zero)
Γ ⊦ [𝟘] 𝟘 ≐ 𝟘 ⇒ 𝕌₀

------------------ (ty-one)
Γ ⊦ [𝟙] 𝟙 ≐ 𝟙 ⇒ 𝕌₀

------------------ (ty-nat)
Γ ⊦ [ℕ] ℕ ≐ ℕ ⇒ 𝕌₀

# Squash

Γ ⊦ [α] t₀ ≐ t₁ ⇐ A
-------------------------- (el-squash-i)
Γ ⊦ [squash α] ⋆ ⇐ ∥A∥

Γ ⊦ [γ] B ⇐ Ω                        // a CHECK at Ω: cumulativity is one-way, B ⇐ 𝕌₀ says nothing
Γ ⊦ [β] ⋆ ⇒ ∥A∥                      // β SYNTHESISES the squash: nothing else determines A
Γ ▷ A ⊦ [α] ⋆ ⇐ B[↑]
------------------------------------- (el-squash-e-prf)
Γ ⊦ [unsquash γ α β] ⋆ ⇒ B

# Ω-type: the propositions

// The prop formers SYNTHESISE Ω whatever the sort of their parts (so the
// impredicative → rule sees them); ⇐ Ω follows by the silent switch.

Γ ⊦ [α] A₀ ≐ A₁ ⇒ 𝒰
------------------------- (code-squash)
Γ ⊦ [∥α∥] ∥A₀∥ ≐ ∥A₁∥ ⇒ Ω

Γ ⊦ [τ] T₀ ≐ T₁ ⇒ 𝒰
Γ ⊦ [α] a₀ ≐ a₁ ⇐ T₁
Γ ⊦ [β] b₀ ≐ b₁ ⇐ T₁
--------------------------------------------------- (code-eq)
Γ ⊦ [α ≡ β ∈ τ] (a₀ ≡ b₀ ∈ T₀) ≐ (a₁ ≡ b₁ ∈ T₁) ⇒ Ω
// At every sort: (A ≡ B ∈ 𝕌ℓ) between types, (p ≡ q ∈ Ω) between
// propositions.

Γ ⊦ [α] a ⇐ T      Γ ⊦ [β] b ⇐ T      T ≡β 𝟙
------------------------------------------------ (el-one-prop)
Γ ⊦ [irrel α β] a ≐ b ⇐ T

Γ ⊦ [α] a ⇐ T      Γ ⊦ [β] b ⇐ T      T ≡β 𝟘
------------------------------------------------ (el-zero-prop)
Γ ⊦ [irrel α β] a ≐ b ⇐ T

Γ ⊦ [γ] T ⇐ Ω      Γ ⊦ [α] a ⇐ T      Γ ⊦ [β] b ⇐ T
----------------------------------------------------- (el-prf-prop)
Γ ⊦ [prop-irrel γ α β] a ≐ b ⇒ T
// γ carries the proposition, so the rule SYNTHESISES it; ⇐ follows
// silently. Propositionhood is witnessed, never read off a core type.

Γ ⊦ [ρ] p ⇐ Ω      Γ ⊦ [θ] q ⇐ Ω      Γ ▷ p ⊦ [γ] s ⇐ q[↑]      Γ ▷ q ⊦ [ι] t ⇐ p[↑]
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ (code-prop-eq)
Γ ⊦ [propext ρ θ γ ι] p ≐ q ⇒ Ω
// Propositional extensionality.

# Modal

Γ ⊦ [α] a₀ ≐ a₁ ⇒ T'
T ≡β T'
--------------------------
Γ ⊦ [α] a₀ ≐ a₁ ⇐ T
// THE SILENT SWITCH, for every α that synthesises: not a leaf but the
// reader's convention. Every proof form belongs to ONE mode, so a
// synthesising form in checking position is read in its own mode and its
// type compared with the expected one; this is what makes Γ ⊦ t ⇐ T
// meaningful for a synthesising t. The switches that change something stay
// explicit: lift (the sort) and the annotation (⇐ to ⇒, the type).

Γ ⊦ [α] a₀ ≐ a₁ ⇒ 𝒰
𝒰 ≤ 𝒰′
-------------------------- (code-lift-eq prop-lift-eq)
Γ ⊦ [lift α] a₀ ≐ a₁ ⇐ 𝒰′
// The switch at a sort: cumulativity, the target sort READ off the
// position; on a term, [lift T] T ≐ T ⇐ 𝒰′.

Γ ⊦ [α] a₀ ≐ a₁ ⇒ 𝒰′
𝒰 ≤ 𝒰′
Γ ⊦ [γ₀] a₀′ ⇐ 𝒰      Γ ⊦ [γ₁] a₁′ ⇐ 𝒰      a₀ ≡β a₀′      a₁ ≡β a₁′
------------------------------------------------------------------- (code-restrict prop-restrict)
Γ ⊦ [restrict γ₀ γ₁ α] a₀ ≐ a₁ ⇐ 𝒰
// MANDATORY: equal types that are codes are equal codes, equal codes that
// are propositions are equivalent propositions — (a₀ ≡ a₁ ∈ 𝒰) and
// (a₀ ≡ a₁ ∈ 𝒰′) equi-true; the sides' membership of 𝒰 is WITNESSED.

Γ ⊦ [β] A ≐ B ⇒ 𝒰
Γ ⊦ [α] t₀ ≐ t₁ ⇐ A
-------------------------- (el-eq-ty-coe)
Γ ⊦ [conv α β] t₀ ≐ t₁ ⇐ B

Γ ⊦ T ⇒ 𝒰
Γ ⊦ [α] t₀ ≐ t₁ ⇐ T
--------------------------
Γ ⊦ [(α : T)] t₀ ≐ t₁ ⇒ T
// Annotation: the switch back, ⇐ to ⇒ — a chain becomes a reify's content,
// a λ a head, an inj a scrutinee; ((conv t α) : T) is the ascription that
// exposes a shape (CONVENTIONS).

# Contextual

---------------------- (el-var)
Γ ⊦ [☐ᵢ] ☐ᵢ ≐ ☐ᵢ ⇒ Γ‖ᵢ

(Δ ⊦ x ≔ t : T) ∈ Σ
[ᾱ] e˲₀ ≐ e˲₁ : Γ ⇒ Δ norm
------------------------------------- (el-sig-var) // el-sig-var in full: the arguments are a NORMAL SUBSTITUTION
Γ ⊦ [x ᾱ] x[e˲₀] ≐ x[e˲₁] ⇒ T[e˲₁]    //   into the item's context

(Δ ⊦ x : T) ∈ Σ
[ᾱ] e˲₀ ≐ e˲₁ : Γ ⇒ Δ norm
------------------------------------- (el-sig-decl) // a declaration alike
Γ ⊦ [x ᾱ] x[e˲₀] ≐ x[e˲₁] ⇒ T[e˲₁]

(Δ ⊦ x ≔ t : T) ∈ Σ
e˲ : Γ ⇒ Δ norm
----------------------------------- (el-sig-beta)
Γ ⊦ [δ x e˲] x[e˲] ≐ t[e˲] ⇒ T[e˲]
// δ is always manual.

# Transitivity, symmetry, let

Γ ⊦ [α] a₀ ≐ a₁ ⇐ T
Γ ⊦ [β] a₁' ≐ a₂ ⇐ T
a₁ ≡β a₁'
----------------------- (el-trans)
Γ ⊦ [α ; β] a₀ ≐ a₂ ⇐ T

Γ ⊦ [α] a₀ ≐ a₁ ⇐ T
----------------------- (el-sym)
Γ ⊦ [α ⁻¹] a₁ ≐ a₀ ⇐ T

Γ ⊦ [α] a₀ ≐ a₁ ⇒ A
Γ ▷ A ▷ (☐₀ ≡ a₁[↑] ∈ A[↑]) ⊦ [β] b₀ ≐ b₁ ⇒ B
-------------------------------------------------- (el-let)
Γ ⊦ [let α β] let a₀ b₀ ≐ let a₁ b₁ ⇒ B[id, a₁, ⋆]

# Leaves: η

// The η's are LEAVES; extensionality is derived:
//   ext(g₀, g₁, α) ≜ (η→ g₀)⁻¹ ; λ α ; η→ g₁     for Γ ▷ A ⊦ [α] g₀[↑] ☐₀ ≐ g₁[↑] ☐₀ ⇐ B
//   likewise at pairs through η× and [α, β], and at records through
//   ηRec and ⟨l̄ ↪ ᾱ⟩.

Γ ⊦ [φ] f ⇐ A → B
------------------------------------ (el-pi-eta)
Γ ⊦ [η→ φ] f ≐ λ (f[↑] ☐₀) ⇐ A → B

Γ ⊦ [π] p ⇐ A × B
------------------------------------- (el-sigma-eta)
Γ ⊦ [η× π] p ≐ (p .π₁, p .π₂) ⇐ A × B

Γ ⊦ [ρ] r ⇐ Rec l̄ Δ
--------------------------------------------------- (el-rec-eta)
Γ ⊦ [ηRec ρ] r ≐ ⟨l̄ ↪ r.l₀, …, r.lₙ₋₁⟩ ⇐ Rec l̄ Δ
// l̄ = l₀ … lₙ₋₁. At the empty record every element is ⟨⟩: a unit type, by
// this leaf.

// Uniqueness of ℕ-elim, ⊎-elim and quot-elim (el-nat-eta, el-sum-eta,
// el-quot-eta) gets NO leaf: it is proved by elimination into the
// equality type and reflected, as the corpus does.

// No injectivity selectors, for now (ty-rec-inj included).

# Polynomials and ν

// The polynomial 𝔽 is CARRIED by the core (ν 𝔽, corec 𝔽 f x): β reads
// it (el-nu-beta consumes map_𝔽). The carrier code a is read by
// typing only, so it is SURFACE — the binder annotation of the
// coalgebra, corec 𝔽 (s : a. f) x — and absent from the core. The
// meta-operations ⌊𝔽⌋(c) (hole filling), map_𝔽 g (functorial action)
// and lift_𝔽(R) (the relator) are the foundation's ≜-definitions,
// computed by the checker; "modulo β" everywhere includes el-nu-beta
// (out of a corec runs the coalgebra one step), as it includes the
// ι-rules and let-β. A polynomial INFERS its least level, the join of
// the sorts its embedded codes infer (|Ω| = 0: a proposition costs
// nothing); ν 𝔽 lives at that level, and a corec's carrier is checked
// at it.

-------------------- (poly-hole)
Γ ⊦ [𝕏] 𝕏 ≐ 𝕏 poly 0

Γ ⊦ [α] a₀ ≐ a₁ ⇒ 𝒰
-------------------------- (poly-const)
Γ ⊦ [K α] K a₀ ≐ K a₁ poly |𝒰|

Γ ⊦ [φ] 𝔽₀ ≐ 𝔽₁ poly ℓ      Γ ⊦ [ψ] 𝔾₀ ≐ 𝔾₁ poly ℓ′
-------------------------------------------------- (poly-prod poly-sum)
Γ ⊦ [φ × ψ] 𝔽₀ × 𝔾₀ ≐ 𝔽₁ × 𝔾₁ poly (ℓ ⊔ ℓ′)
Γ ⊦ [φ ⊎ ψ] 𝔽₀ ⊎ 𝔾₀ ≐ 𝔽₁ ⊎ 𝔾₁ poly (ℓ ⊔ ℓ′)

Γ ⊦ [α] a₀ ≐ a₁ ⇒ 𝒰      Γ ▷ a₁ ⊦ [φ] 𝔽₀ ≐ 𝔽₁ poly ℓ
---------------------------------------------------- (poly-sigma poly-pi)
Γ ⊦ [α × φ] a₀ × 𝔽₀ ≐ a₁ × 𝔽₁ poly (|𝒰| ⊔ ℓ)
Γ ⊦ [α → φ] a₀ → 𝔽₀ ≐ a₁ → 𝔽₁ poly (|𝒰| ⊔ ℓ)

Γ ⊦ [φ] 𝔽₀ ≐ 𝔽₁ poly ℓ
------------------------- (ty-nu)
Γ ⊦ [ν φ] ν 𝔽₀ ≐ ν 𝔽₁ ⇒ 𝕌ℓ

Γ ⊦ [α] t₀ ≐ t₁ ⇒ ν 𝔽
---------------------------------- (el-nu-e)
Γ ⊦ [out α] out t₀ ≐ out t₁ ⇒ ⌊𝔽⌋(ν 𝔽)

Γ ⊦ 𝔽 poly ℓ      Γ ⊦ a ⇐ 𝕌ℓ
Γ ▷ a ⊦ [φ] f₀ ≐ f₁ ⇐ ⌊𝔽⌋(a)[↑]
Γ ⊦ [χ] x₀ ≐ x₁ ⇐ a
-------------------------------------------------------------------- (el-nu-i)
Γ ⊦ [corec 𝔽 (s : a. φ) χ] corec 𝔽 f₀ x₀ ≐ corec 𝔽 f₁ x₁ ⇒ ν 𝔽
// Same 𝔽: a corec at an equal polynomial goes through ν φ and conversion
// of the equation.

## Leaves: uniqueness and coinduction

Γ ⊦ 𝔽 poly ℓ      Γ ⊦ a ⇐ 𝕌ℓ
Γ ▷ a ⊦ f ⇐ ⌊𝔽⌋(a)[↑]
Γ ▷ a ⊦ h ⇐ (ν 𝔽)[↑]
Γ ▷ a ⊦ [α] out h ≐ map_𝔽 ((λ h)[↑]) f ⇐ ⌊𝔽⌋(ν 𝔽)[↑]
Γ ⊦ x ⇐ a
------------------------------------------------------------ (el-nu-eta)
Γ ⊦ [ην 𝔽 (s : a. f) (s. h) α x] h[id, x] ≐ corec 𝔽 f x ⇒ ν 𝔽
// A candidate commuting with out IS the corecursor.

Γ ⊦ t₀ ⇐ ν 𝔽      Γ ⊦ t₁ ⇐ ν 𝔽                                 // 𝔽 the input type's polynomial
Γ ▷ ν 𝔽 ▷ (ν 𝔽)[↑] ⊦ R ⇐ Ω
Γ ⊦ p ⇐ R[id, t₀, t₁]
Γ ▷ ν 𝔽 ▷ (ν 𝔽)[↑] ▷ R ⊦ q ⇐ lift_𝔽(R) (out ☐₂) (out ☐₁)
------------------------------------------------------------ (el-nu-coind) // el-nu-coind: bisimulation implies
Γ ⊦ [coind t₀ t₁ (x y. R) p (x y h. q)] t₀ ≐ t₁ ⇐ ν 𝔽        //   equality; admissible from ην,
                                                             //   kept as the leaf the corpus writes

# QIITs

// A signature is a qiit-context Φ, DEFINED ONCE as an item
// (Δ ⊦ x ≔ Φ qsig ℓ) of Σ over its parameters Δ. A core term carries the
// item's NAME and arguments for its parameters, never a context:
// x[e˲].𝕤 ē, x[e˲].𝕔 θ, x[e˲].𝕤-elim m̄ ē w. QIIT equality is NOMINAL — one
// item at equal arguments, the foundation's qsig-eq-ref — which is
// conservative and incomplete (THE FRAGMENT, at the end); β reads the
// item (el-qiit-beta recurses by the constructor's arity). A context is
// WRITTEN in the theory of signatures below — the grammar is the
// positivity guarantee, and β reads constructor arities off it — and it
// is TYPED through its reading as a Nova telescope, ⟦Φ⟧, over the
// ALGEBRA CONTEXT Δ · ⟦Φ⟧: an algebra is a spine of that telescope; the
// initial algebra ι is the spine of the formers themselves; the
// eliminator's motives, methods and coherences are ONE spine of the
// displayed telescope ⟦Φ⟧ᴰ over ι; the eliminator's type and its β are
// substitutions. Nothing about the ToS is trusted beyond the readings
// ⟦_⟧ and _ᴰ and the displayed spine θᴰ, each defined by recursion on
// the grammar and landing in Nova syntax the rules above already read.
// The eliminator's core carries the METHODS only: motives, coherences
// and the sorts 𝒰̄ the motives land in are SURFACE, as ℕ-elim's A and 𝒰
// are.

// A signature is checked AT A LEVEL ℓ, its BOUND: every Nova type it
// embeds at 𝕌ℓ (a proposition included, by Ω ≤ 𝕌₀ ≤ 𝕌ℓ), its sorts
// types at 𝕌ℓ, ⟦Φ⟧ a telescope with sort entries at 𝕌ℓ₊₁. One bound
// serves every sort: one check at 𝕌ℓ, no universe guessed.

// (Telescopes, spines and the derived snoc the readings build with:
// LISTS, after the entry points.)

## The theory of signatures (surface = core: nameless indexed syntax)

// The syntax of qiit-contexts Φ, qiit-types 𝔄 and qiit-terms 𝕥 is the
// foundation's (THEORY OF SIGNATURES — grammar, in its QIIT section). A
// SIGNATURE here is a closed qiit-context, the definiens of an item.
// What follows is how the kernel CHECKS one: the modes, and the level.

Γ ⊦ Φ qctx ℓ           // Given core Γ, check surface Φ at level ℓ (elaborating its Nova pieces). Run ONCE per
                       //   signature, at its item (the entry points). An embedded Nova piece is a ONE-SIDED
                       //   proof: its sides β-join and the right one is recorded. There is NO equation of
                       //   contexts: two formers are compared by the name of their item and its arguments
Γ ; Φ ⊦ 𝔄 qty ℓ
Γ ; Φ ⊦ 𝕥 ⇒ 𝔄          // ToS terms INFER: they are variables and application chains
Γ ; Φ ⊦ 𝕥 ⇐ 𝔄

------------ (qctx-empty)
Γ ⊦ ⬦ qctx ℓ

Γ ⊦ Φ qctx ℓ      Γ ; Φ ⊦ 𝔄 qty ℓ
---------------------------------- (qctx-ext)
Γ ⊦ Φ ▷ 𝔄 qctx ℓ

Γ ⊦ Φ qctx ℓ
----------------- (qty-univ)
Γ ; Φ ⊦ U qty ℓ

Γ ; Φ ⊦ 𝕥 ⇐ U
---------------- (qty-el)
Γ ; Φ ⊦ El 𝕥 qty ℓ

Γ ⊦ A ⇐ 𝕌ℓ      Γ ▷ A ; Φ[↑] ⊦ 𝔄 qty ℓ
------------------------------------- (qty-pi-ext)
Γ ; Φ ⊦ A ⇛ 𝔄 qty ℓ

Γ ; Φ ⊦ 𝕥 ⇐ U      Γ ; Φ ▷ El 𝕥 ⊦ 𝔄 qty ℓ
---------------------------------------- (qty-pi-ind)
Γ ; Φ ⊦ El 𝕥 ⇛ 𝔄 qty ℓ

---------------- (qtm-var)
Γ ; Φ ⊦ ⬡ᵢ ⇒ Φ‖ᵢ

Γ ; Φ ⊦ 𝕥 ⇒ A ⇛ 𝔄      Γ ⊦ t ⇐ A
---------------------------------- (qtm-app-ext)
Γ ; Φ ⊦ 𝕥 t ⇒ 𝔄[id, t]

Γ ; Φ ⊦ 𝕥 ⇒ El 𝕦 ⇛ 𝔄      Γ ; Φ ⊦ 𝕥' ⇐ El 𝕦
------------------------------------------- (qtm-app-ind)
Γ ; Φ ⊦ 𝕥 𝕥' ⇒ 𝔄[𝕥']

Γ ▷ A ; Φ[↑] ⊦ 𝕥 ⇐ 𝔄
------------------------ (qtm-lam-ext)
Γ ; Φ ⊦ λ 𝕥 ⇐ A ⇛ 𝔄

Γ ; Φ ⊦ 𝕥₀ ⇐ El 𝕦      Γ ; Φ ⊦ 𝕥₁ ⇐ El 𝕦
------------------------------------------ (qtm-eq)
Γ ; Φ ⊦ 𝕥₀ ≡ 𝕥₁ ⇐ U

Γ ; Φ ⊦ 𝕥 ⇒ 𝔄'      𝔄 ≡β 𝔄'
------------------------- // mode switch (β on the embedded Nova pieces only)
Γ ; Φ ⊦ 𝕥 ⇐ 𝔄

## The readings ⟦_⟧ and _ᴰ

// The reading of a qiit-context as a telescope ⟦Φ⟧ over Γ, and of its
// types and terms over the algebra context Γ · ⟦Φ⟧; the arity telescope
// ⟦𝔄⟧ᵗ and end ⟦𝔄⟧ᵉ of an entry; and the displayed reading 𝔄ᴰ, 𝕥ᴰ, ⟦Φ⟧ᴰ
// over Γ · ⟦Φ⟧ · ⟦Φ⟧ᴰ — all are the foundation's, clause for clause (its
// QIIT section: THE READING, An ARITY, THE DISPLAYED READING), and they
// are what the kernel computes. The displayed reading's TARGETS 𝒰̄, one
// per sort of Φ, each Ω or a universe, are sorts, and the eliminator
// NAMES them: 𝒰_𝕤 is the sort its motive for 𝕤 lands in (CONVENTIONS:
// eliminators name their sort).

// A FORMER names an item (Δ ⊦ x ≔ Φ qsig ℓ) ∈ Σ and instantiates its
// parameters by a normal substitution e˲ : Γ ⇒ Δ norm, as a reference to
// a term item does. The readings are taken of Φ over Δ, the item's own
// context, and a former's types are their INSTANCES, by substitution.
// (The foundation's content of the reference, ⌈x[e˲]⌉, is Φ[e˲], and a
// reading commutes with the substitution.) An ALGEBRA of x at e˲ over Γ
// is a spine Γ ⊦ ā ⇐ ⟦Φ⟧[e˲]. The INITIAL algebra Γ ⊦ ι ⇐ ⟦Φ⟧[e˲] is the
// spine of the formers at x[e˲], entry by entry (e˲ weakened under the
// λs):

ι(𝕤)  = λ ⟦𝔎⟧ᵗ[e˲, ι]. x[e˲].𝕤 (the bound variables)    // for a sort entry Φ(𝕤) = 𝔎
ι(𝕔)  = λ ⟦𝔄⟧ᵗ[e˲, ι]. x[e˲].𝕔 (the bound variables)    // for a point entry Φ(𝕔) = 𝔄
ι(𝕔)  = λ ⟦𝔄⟧ᵗ[e˲, ι]. ⋆                              // for an equation entry: its end is a proposition

// Every type below is stated in the algebra context Δ · ⟦Φ⟧ and
// instantiated at the parameters and the initial algebra by
// substitution: X[e˲, ι] is X[(e˲, ι)], the substitution e˲ : Γ ⇒ Δ
// extended by the spine ι, and X[e˲, ι, θ] extends it by a further
// spine.

// ⟦Φ⟧ᴰ[e˲, ι] is the telescope of the eliminator's SURFACE arguments in
// signature order — motives at the sort entries, methods at the point
// entries, coherences at the equation entries — and Γ ⊦ d̄ ⇐ ⟦Φ⟧ᴰ[e˲, ι]
// is all of them at once. d̄(𝕤) names the motive entry for sort 𝕤, d̄(𝕔)
// the method entry for point 𝕔, m̄ the point entries (what the core
// keeps).

## The outer formers

// Each names an item (Δ ⊦ x ≔ Φ qsig ℓ) ∈ Σ. A sort and a point
// constructor are congruent in the reference's arguments — NOMINAL
// equality: one item, equal arguments — and their types are instances
// at the RIGHT ones, as every type is built from the right side. The
// eliminator and the path leaf are at ONE substitution e˲. ι is the
// initial algebra at the arguments the types are instantiated by.

(Δ ⊦ x ≔ Φ qsig ℓ) ∈ Σ      [π̄] e˲₀ ≐ e˲₁ : Γ ⇒ Δ norm
Φ(𝕤) = 𝔎      Γ ⊦ [ᾱ] ē₀ ≐ ē₁ ⇐ ⟦𝔎⟧ᵗ[e˲₁, ι]
---------------------------------------------------- (ty-qiit ty-qiit-cong qsig-eq-ref)
Γ ⊦ [x[π̄].𝕤 ᾱ] x[e˲₀].𝕤 ē₀ ≐ x[e˲₁].𝕤 ē₁ ⇒ 𝕌ℓ
// ty-qiit in full (ty-qiit-cong, by qsig-eq-ref): a sort is a type at the
// level its item records. The spine equation is at the arity instantiated
// by ē₁'s prefix.

(Δ ⊦ x ≔ Φ qsig ℓ) ∈ Σ      [π̄] e˲₀ ≐ e˲₁ : Γ ⇒ Δ norm
Φ(𝕔) = 𝔄      𝔄 ends El 𝕥      Γ ⊦ [ᾱ] θ₀ ≐ θ₁ ⇐ ⟦𝔄⟧ᵗ[e˲₁, ι]
------------------------------------------------------------ (el-qiit-intro el-qiit-intro-cong)
Γ ⊦ [x[π̄].𝕔 ᾱ] x[e˲₀].𝕔 θ₀ ≐ x[e˲₁].𝕔 θ₁ ⇒ ⟦𝕥⟧[e˲₁, ι, θ₁]
// el-qiit-intro in full, SATURATED.

(Δ ⊦ x ≔ Φ qsig ℓ) ∈ Σ      e˲ : Γ ⇒ Δ norm      𝒰̄ targets Φ
Γ ⊦ [δ̄] d̄₀ ≐ d̄₁ ⇐ ⟦Φ⟧ᴰ[e˲, ι]                        // motives, methods, coherences: ONE spine of the displayed
Φ(𝕤) = 𝔎      Γ ⊦ [ᾱ] ē₀ ≐ ē₁ ⇐ ⟦𝔎⟧ᵗ[e˲, ι]           //   telescope over the initial algebra. Entrywise: the motive
Γ ⊦ [κ] w₀ ≐ w₁ ⇐ x[e˲].𝕤 ē₁                         //   entries reflexive (the two eliminators share their
--------------------------------------------------- (el-qiit-elim) //   motives), the method entries proper equations, a
Γ ⊦ [x[e˲].𝕤-elim 𝒰̄ δ̄ ᾱ κ]                           //   coherence entry a proposition (irrel at 𝒰_𝕤 = Ω, a proof
    x[e˲].𝕤-elim m̄₀ ē₀ w₀ ≐ x[e˲].𝕤-elim m̄₁ ē₁ w₁     //   otherwise). Core: x[e˲].𝕤-elim m̄ ē w, m̄ the point entries
    ⇒ d̄₁(𝕤) ē₁ᴰ w₁                                  //   of d̄; ēᴰ the DISPLAYED SPINE of the indices (COMPUTATION
                                                    //   below). ONE e˲: across equal arguments, go through
                                                    //   the sort's congruence and conversion

// COMPUTATION is el-qiit-beta, inside "modulo β": at a constructor
// Φ(𝕔) = 𝔄 with arguments Γ ⊦ θ ⇐ ⟦𝔄⟧ᵗ[e˲, ι],
//   x[e˲].𝕤-elim m̄ ⟦ī⟧[e˲, ι, θ] (x[e˲′].𝕔 θ)  ⇝  m_𝕔 θᴰ
// when the eliminator and the constructor agree NOMINALLY — one item,
// the arguments e˲ and e˲′ equal modulo β — where Γ ⊦ θᴰ ⇐ ⟦𝔄⟧ᵗᴰ[e˲, ι, d̄] is
// the DISPLAYED SPINE of θ (likewise ēᴰ of an index spine
// Γ ⊦ ē ⇐ ⟦𝔎⟧ᵗ[e˲, ι] in the eliminator's type): entrywise, an external
// argument a ↦ a, an internal argument u : x[e˲].𝕤′ ī′ ↦ u,
// x[e˲].𝕤′-elim m̄ ī′ u (the eliminator itself at the recursive position:
// the section φᵉˡ), an internal argument at an equation code ↦ u
// alone. Equation constructors have no β: their content is the path
// leaf below.

## Leaves

(Δ ⊦ x ≔ Φ qsig ℓ) ∈ Σ      e˲ : Γ ⇒ Δ norm
Φ(𝕔) = 𝔄      𝔄 ends El (𝕝 ≡ 𝕣) at 𝕦      Γ ⊦ θ ⇐ ⟦𝔄⟧ᵗ[e˲, ι]
------------------------------------------------------------------------------ (el-qiit-path)
Γ ⊦ [x[e˲].𝕔 θ] ⟦𝕝⟧[e˲, ι, θ] ≐ ⟦𝕣⟧[e˲, ι, θ] ⇒ ⟦𝕦⟧[e˲, ι, θ]
// The imposed equation, as a proof leaf (no term is minted: the prop's
// element is ⋆).

// Uniqueness (el-qiit-eta) gets no leaf, as at ℕ, ⊎ and / (ν's ην is
// the one exception): the corpus proves it by elimination into the
// equality type and reflection. No constructor injectivity: equation
// entries make constructors non-injective in general (quotients); no
// index selector either, for now.

## The fragment

// Equality of QIIT formers here is NOMINAL: the same item
// at equal arguments, and nothing else. That is CONSERVATIVE — every
// equation the kernel accepts is the foundation's by-name pathway,
// qsig-eq-ref — and INCOMPLETE: the foundation also lets a former carry
// a signature written out, lets an item be defined by a reference (an
// alias, an instance), and equates signatures by content. The kernel
// has none of the three. Its syntax has no signature beside the context
// an item defines; a core term holds a name and its arguments; and two items
// with the same content are unrelated. What the content pathway would
// give back is had otherwise: a transparent name for one sort of an
// instance is an ordinary definition of that sort, unfolded by δ, and a
// signature under binders is an item over those binders as parameters.
